Possible minor spoiler on AC from enchant armour scrolls.

Someone posted that it was possible to get high armour enchantments because
of the way scrolls of enchant armour work. You can enchant ordinary armour
when it is less than +3 without any risk or an elvish mithril coat
when less than +5. When you are over this enchantment each scroll has
a 1/current enchantment chance of evaporating it. This means that if
you enchant a elven mitril coat, starting at +5 you can get it to +43
with a 50/50 chance of losing it(if all scrolls enchant by 3) or to
about +17 if the scrolls enchant by 1,2 or 3 randomly, again with a 50/50
risk of loss.
Of course this many scrolls may be difficult to find, but it is possible.
For example wait till you are late on in the game(but not into hell)
collect all the wands and scrolls, find a wand of cancellation, zap
it at the scrolls(which now become blank and will group) bless the scrolls
with a potion of holy water. Then zap the wand of poly at the pile, picking
out any wands of poly that are generated. Eventually you will have a lot
of blessed enchant armour scrolls(genocide and enchant weapon scrolls
can also be made). Now enchant a elven mithril coat to +5 and keep reading
enchant armour scrolls on it till you get chicken or the AC gets to a
unreasonable level. The most risk is taken at the start, when a run of
scrolls enchanting by 3 will greatly reduce the chance of it being vaped,
but a few enchanting by 1 will greatly increase the chance.
Let me know if this works for anybody in a real game.

(I'm not going to try this on my current game, I have -49 armour and -49
intrinsic AC(from priestess while a leprechaun) so I don't need it)

